description:
A strip of controls with one tab stop: the arrow keys move between its items along `orientation:`, Home / End jump to the ends. Too many items scroll instead of wrapping.

  Toolbar(aria_label: "Formatting") do
    ToolbarGroup(aria_label: "Text style") do
      ToolbarButton { |item| Button(**item, variant: :ghost) { "Bold" } }
      ToolbarButton { |item| Button(**item, variant: :ghost) { "Italic" } }
    end
    ToolbarSeparator()
    ToolbarLink(href: "#help") { "Help" }
  end

Items hand their attributes to your own control (ToolbarButton → a Button, a Toggle, a SelectTrigger; ToolbarInput → an Input), so it keeps its look and joins the focus order.

ToolbarButton.description:
A toolbar button. Pass a block with an argument to put the attributes on your own control:

  ToolbarButton { |item| Button(**item, variant: :ghost, icon: true, aria_label: "Bold") { Icon(:bold) } }

Disabled items stay reachable (aria-disabled) so keyboard users can still read them.
